 "business": {
  "status": "ok",
  "overview": [
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 97,
    "excerpt": "Transaprency and Responsiveness Root Cause Analysis Timely Corrective ActionsGlobal Practices Regulatory Requirements Swift Issue Evaluation Robust Recall Framework The Net Promoter Score (NPS) is a globally recognised metric that measures customer loyalty and their likelihood to recommend Maruti Suzuki to others. The NPS for the year stood at 93.4 (Arena 93.9 and NEXA 92.3).",
    "section": "Leadership message"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 39,
    "excerpt": "The Company remained India's leading exporter of passenger vehicles for the fifth consecutive year. Revenue increased to an all-time high of over INR 1.8 lakh crore, with profit after tax about ` 144,454 million also reaching record levels. Consequently, the Board has recommended highest- ever dividend of ` 140 per share.",
    "section": "Leadership message"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 83,
    "excerpt": "Material Circularity Supply chain operations are one of the major contributors to the Company’s overall GHG emissions (Scope 3.1). Steel and aluminium are the two major materials. Therefore,",
    "section": "Leadership message"
   }
  ],
  "segments": null,
  "management": [
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-04",
    "page": 2,
    "excerpt": "Our domestic sales volume growth during the year was constrained by production capacity. As of the end of the fiscal year, around 190,000 customer orders remained unserved, and we are trying to service them fast, highlighting the strength of the underlying demand. Importantly, near 130,000 of these pending orders were in the small car segment, falling in the 18% GST bracket.",
    "speaker": "Rahul Bharti"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-04",
    "page": 4,
    "excerpt": "Importantly, the recent GST reduction is seen as a transformative factor for the passenger vehicle sector in India. By lowering taxes, the reform has enhanced affordability, making passenger vehicles accessible to a broader segment of customers. This, in turn, has set the industry on a path of sustained long-term structural growth by enlarging the potential customer base.",
    "speaker": "Rahul Bharti"
   }
  ]
 },
